# Shared UI foundation

This library is the one application-owned integration boundary for WebQuark.
Every frontend application reuses it instead of creating its own WebQuark
loader, theme, or global overrides.

Integration enabled: `{webquark.integrationEnabled}`.

## Stable layout

- `styles/foundation.css` loads WebQuark base CSS before the application token layer.
- `styles/webquark-theme.css` is the only location for application-wide `--q-*` overrides.
- `src/setup-webquark.ts` exists only when integration is enabled and owns browser loader setup.
- Application layout styles stay application-owned and load after this foundation.
- Reusable wrappers or Shadow Part exceptions belong below this shared library only when they add reusable project meaning or behavior. Do not create them pre-emptively.

Prefer global theme tokens for application-wide changes. Use documented Shadow
Parts only for isolated exceptions; never target private shadow DOM or internal
classes.

## Reuse before replacing

Check this catalogue before creating a new UI primitive. For compact desktop
interfaces, use `size="sm"` when the selected component's public API exposes a
size option.

- Actions: `q-button`, `q-chip`, `q-link`
- Layout and navigation: `q-card`, `q-carousel`, `q-form`, `q-navbar`, `q-panel`, `q-scrollable`, `q-sidepanel`, `q-toolbar`
- Forms: `q-input`, `q-textarea`, `q-dropdown`, `q-quantity-selector`, `q-radio-group`, `q-toggle`
- Data and indicators: `q-conversation-bubble`, `q-data-table`, `q-map`, `q-syntax-box`, `q-circular-progress`, `q-step-diagram`, `q-step-diagram-item`
- Media: `q-avatar`, `q-icon`, `q-reel`, `q-thumbnail`
- Overlays: `q-dialog`, `q-toast`, `q-tooltip`

For behavior and API details, consult WebQuark's `docs/components/README.md`,
the matching `docs/components/q-*.md` guide, generated
`src/components/**/readme.md`, `docs/theme_variables.md`, and the installed
`@webquark/core` TypeScript declarations. Generated API and declarations win
when prose and the installed version disagree. The canonical source is
<https://github.com/Purely-IT/WebQuark>.
